The  utility acts as a frontend to the library, allowing mounting
and unmounting of refuse‐based file systems.   There  are  essen‐
tially  two forms of the command.  The first, and default option,
is to mount a refuse‐based file system.  By using  the  argument,
the  file  system can be unmounted.  The arguments to are as fol‐
lows: Set a flag to enable kernel caching of files.   At  present
this  option has no effect.  Make the name argument appear as the
file system name in and output.  Print a usage message and  exit.
Check  the  file  permissions.  At present this option has no ef‐
fect.  Display the version on stdout, and then exit successfully.
Allow mortal (non‐root) users to  access  the  file  system.   At
present,  this  option  has  no  effect.  The utility is included
mainly for compatibility reasons, since some file systems  demand
its  existence.   returns 0 for successful operation, or non‐zero
